      "math_academy_id": "q-181629",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "$$\nC={1,2,…,100},\\,D={2n∣\\,n\\in Z}\n$$\n\nComplete the following reasoning about the sets $C$ and $D$ above:\n\nSince $C$ is {{field-1}} and $D$ is {{field-2}}, we have that {{field-3}}.",
